<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shikanoshima</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shikanoshima is a small island at the mouth of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hakata">Hakata</a> Bay in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fukuoka">Fukuoka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, joined to the mainland by a sandbar. In 1784 a farmer found there a gold seal inscribed 'King of Na of Wa of Han', generally identified with the seal the Chinese emperor Guangwu granted to envoys from Na in 57 CE. The seal, now a National Treasure, is one of the earliest objects linking Japan to written history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shikanoshima.jpg" alt="Shikanoshima" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 厄無し / Yakunashi · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shikano-shima_island_from_Hakata_bay.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
